        "message": {
          "content": "A) Take the $5,000\n\n**Explanation:** \nThe decision rests on which outcome produces the greatest overall balance of well-being and minimizes net suffering. Because of the diminishing marginal utility of money, $5,000 provides vastly more relief to someone facing months of severe financial strain, mounting debt, and deprivation than the harm it causes to a person who can absorb the loss from savings and merely postpones a luxury vacation. Since there is no risk of detection, punishment, or an innocent third party being blamed, the overall net positive impact on human welfare is higher if the money is taken.",
